<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia Yield Spreads-Underperform post-tender.</title>
<headline>Australia Yield Spreads-Underperform post-tender.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> AUD VS   3-YR	   10-YR	* AUD 3-YR/10-YR SPREAD</p>
<p> USD	-22 (+ 08)    42 (+ 06) * FUTURES    69  (- 00.5)</p>
<p> CAD	 74 (+ 05)    62 (+ 03) * CASH	 88  (- 01)</p>
<p> NZD     -152 (- 01)   -31 (+ 03) *</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Australian bonds underperformed against the dollar bloc as the market continued to mark time ahead of next week's Reserve Bank board meeting.  </p>
<p>Traders said the market was largely consolidating after today's A$500 million Treasury bond tender, and with the downside for yields fairly limited until the expected 50 basis point easing in official rates becomes reality.</p>
<p>U.S. Treasuries rallied on Monday in anticipation of a favourable outcome to the second quarter employment costs index due later on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The New Zealand debt market made a partial recovery in tandem with the N.Z. dollar, having both weakened again in early trading.</p>
<p>-- Colin Brinsden 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
